s2-1-p10 : Block
s2-1-p10 = prose (cons "The difference between a *proposition* and a general type matters. A proposition has at most one inhabitant up to equality; a type may carry many distinct values and nontrivial higher paths. When the only question is whether a witness exists, propositional truncation discards which witness it was. When a witness must be executed, transformed, or transported, discarding it is an irreversible change of information. The type discipline lets that choice be stated exactly." nil)
